Packed argMax and argMin implementation (#1574)

PERF

- Packed arg reduce doesn't do (expensive) reshape of tensors to and from 2D, like done in non-packed operation variant. Previous stages of this PR implement that kind of approach (reshape to 2D before op and reshape output back) and there is no performance improvement.
- Add and modify argMax and argMin tests to cover tensors of different ranks.
- Vectorize comparison and assignment.
- This patch implements packed support for tensors of rank greater than 2.
 
Performance improvement is measured [by benchmark](https://gist.github.com/astojilj/b1185e799f1a8f952d820a85957b7b93) on integrated GPU Intel® Iris™ Pro 5200 on MacBook Pro (Retina, 15-inch, Mid 2014). argMax(-1) of (packed) tensor of shape [1, 513, 513, 21] to result [1, 513, 513] is final operation of semantic segmentation DeepLabV3+ MobileNetV2 model (21 classes segmentation). This operation, with packed input tensors of different sizes, is used in the [benchmark](https://gist.github.com/astojilj/b1185e799f1a8f952d820a85957b7b93#file-packedreducebenchmark-patch-L61):

```
argMax input       |    master    |  with the patch
--------------------------------------------------
[1, 257, 257, 21]  |    12.2ms    |     6.7ms
[1, 513, 513, 21]  |    34.1ms    |    15.4ms
[1, 769, 769, 21]  |    69.9ms    |    31.3ms
```

Compiled userCode for
```
    const a = tf.tensor3d([3, 2, 5, 100, -7, 2], [2, 1, 3]);
    const r = tf.argMax(a, -1);
```
is:

```
      float getAChannel(int x,int y,int z) {
        return getChannel(getA(x,y,z),
                               vec2(y,z));
      }
      
      void main() {
        ivec2 coords = getOutputCoords();
        bool hasNextCol = coords.y < 0;
        bool hasNextRow = coords.x < 0;
        
        ivec3 sourceLocR = ivec3(coords.x,coords.y, 0);
        ++coords.y;
        ivec3 sourceLocG = ivec3(coords.x,coords.y, 0);
        ++coords.x;
        ivec3 sourceLocA = ivec3(coords.x,coords.y, 0);
        --coords.y;
        ivec3 sourceLocB = ivec3(coords.x,coords.y, 0);
        --coords.x;
        ivec4 srcIdx = ivec4(sourceLocR.z, sourceLocG.z,
          sourceLocB.z, sourceLocA.z) * 3;
        ivec4 inIdx = srcIdx;
        vec4 bestIndex = vec4(inIdx);
        vec4 bestValue = vec4(
            getAChannel(sourceLocR.x,sourceLocR.y,inIdx.r),
            hasNextCol ? getAChannel(sourceLocG.x,sourceLocG.y,inIdx.g) : 0.,
            hasNextRow ? getAChannel(sourceLocB.x,sourceLocB.y,inIdx.b) : 0.,
            hasNextRow && hasNextCol ? getAChannel(sourceLocA.x,sourceLocA.y,inIdx.a) : 0.);

        for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
          inIdx = srcIdx;
          
          vec4 candidate = vec4(
            getAChannel(sourceLocR.x,sourceLocR.y,inIdx.r),
            hasNextCol ? getAChannel(sourceLocG.x,sourceLocG.y,inIdx.g) : 0.,
            hasNextRow ? getAChannel(sourceLocB.x,sourceLocB.y,inIdx.b) : 0.,
            hasNextRow && hasNextCol ? getAChannel(sourceLocA.x,sourceLocA.y,inIdx.a) : 0.);
          bvec4 nan = isNaN(candidate);
          bvec4 replace = bvec4(
            vec4(greaterThan(candidate, bestValue)) * (vec4(1.0) - vec4(nan)));

          bestValue = vec4(replace.x  ? candidate.x : bestValue.x,
                           replace.y  ? candidate.y : bestValue.y,
                           replace.z  ? candidate.z : bestValue.z,
                           replace.w  ? candidate.w : bestValue.w);
          bestIndex = mix(bestIndex, vec4(inIdx), vec4(replace));
          srcIdx++;
        }
        setOutput(bestIndex);
      }
```

