Fix onProgress for http url in loadLayersModel (#544)

BUG

Issue [tensorflow/tfjs#1610](https://github.com/tensorflow/tfjs/issues/1610) pointed out that `onProgress` callback of tf.loadGraphModel breaks when using HTTP url. While I found that it also breaks in tf.loadLayersModel, for example:

```javascript
// onProgress works
const model = await tf.loadLayersModel('./PATH/TO/MODEL/model.json', {
  onProgress: function(fraction) {
    console.log(fraction);
  }
});
```

```javascript
// onProgress breaks
const model = await tf.loadLayersModel('https://URL/TO/MODEL/model.json', {
  onProgress: function(fraction) {
    console.log(fraction);
  }
});
```
This PR passes `onProgress` to io.getLoadHandlers to fix the bug.

**Note:**
This PR depends on [tensorflow/tfjs-core#1769](https://github.com/tensorflow/tfjs-core/pull/1769)

